Interest Rate Risk *(IRR)* is the risk that the value of an investment will decrease due to *changes in the absolute level of interest rates*, in the *spread* between two rates, in the *shape of the yield curve*, or in *any other interest rate relationship*.

Which may cause a decline in the value of interest-rate-sensitive portfolios

Interest Rate Risk is considered a type of #voir("market-risk")